  "instruction": "Give me a list of all of the fish that Albacore form mixed schools with, but ignore the ones that can live over 20 years.",
  "answer": "Based on the research, here are the fish that form mixed schools with Albacore and live 20 years or less:\n\n## Fish that school with Albacore (lifespan ≤ 20 years)\n\n| Common Name | Scientific Name | Max Recorded Age | Schooling Source | Lifespan Source |\n|-------------|-----------------|------------------|------------------|-----------------|\n| **Skipjack tuna** | *Katsuwonus pelamis* | 12 years | FAO Species Catalogue Vol. 2 (Collette & Nauen 1983), FishBase, NOAA Fisheries, Animal Diversity Web | FishBase Ref. 168 |\n| **Yellowfin tuna** | *Thunnus albacares* | 18 years | FAO Species Catalogue Vol. 2 (Collette & Nauen 1983), FishBase, NOAA Fisheries, Animal Diversity Web | FishBase Ref. 137697 |\n\n## Excluded species (lifespan > 20 years)\n\n- **Southern bluefin tuna** (*Thunnus maccoyii*) — documented mixed-school associate per FishBase/FAO, but maximum age 20–40 years (FishBase, Gunn et al. 2008)\n\n## Notes\n\n- The three consistently documented mixed-school associates across FAO, NOAA, FishBase, and Animal Diversity Web are **Skipjack, Yellowfin, and Southern bluefin tuna**.\n- Other species (Bigeye, Blackfin, Longtail, Frigate, Bullet, Kawakawa, Mahi-mahi, Wahoo, Rainbow runner, Triggerfish) were not confirmed as Albacore mixed-school associates in the authoritative sources searched.\n- Mixed schools typically involve **juvenile/immature Albacore** and often associate with **floating objects** (Sargassum, FADs).\n\n## Sources\n\n1. https://fishbase.se/summary/Speciessummary.php?id=142\n2. https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Thunnus_alalunga\n3. https://www.fisheries.noaa.gov/species/north-atlantic-albacore-tuna\n4. https://www.vliz.be/imisdocs/publications/307984.pdf\n5. https://www.fishbase.se/summary/katsuwonus-pelamis.html\n6. https://www.fishbase.se/summary/thunnus-albacares.html\n7. https://www.fishbase.se/summary/Thunnus-maccoyii.html",
